### **STEP 4 — Add Function Node to Parse the Data**

Drag a **Function** node, connect it after the HTTP Request, and paste this code:

```javascript
try {
    if (typeof msg.payload === "string") {
        msg.payload = JSON.parse(msg.payload);
    }

    const rows = msg.payload.values;
    if (!rows || rows.length < 2) {
        node.warn("No data found in sheet");
        return null;
    }

    const headers = rows[0];
    const records = rows.slice(1).map(r => {
        const obj = {};
        headers.forEach((h, i) => obj[h] = r[i] || "");
        return obj;
    });

    msg.payload = records;
    return msg;

} catch (err) {
    node.error("JSON parse error: " + err.message, msg);
}
```

